<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Saint Vincent</h1><p class="st-meta">1763 CE – 1979 CE · capital Kingstown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British colony on Saint Vincent, taken from its Garifuna inhabitants by war and deportation, known for arrowroot, breadfruit and La Soufrière volcano.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-vincent-island">Saint Vincent</a> was largely held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garifuna">Garifuna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1763">Treaty of Paris</a> of 1763 granted it to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>. Surveyors began dividing land for plantations, provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-carib-war">First Carib War</a> of 1772 to 1773. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied the island from 1779 to 1783, and in 1795 to 1796 the Garifuna rose again before their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> in 1797.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A governor, council and assembly ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingstown">Kingstown</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and later arrowroot were grown on estates worked by enslaved Africans. The botanic garden founded in 1765 is among the oldest in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh">William Bligh's</a> breadfruit in 1793. After emancipation, indentured workers came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madeira">Madeira</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The assembly gave way to crown colony rule in 1877, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-soufriere-saint-vincent">La Soufrière</a>'s eruption in 1902 killed about 1,600 people.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-vincent-island">Saint Vincent</a> belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-windward-islands">British Windward Islands</a>, then joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-indies-federation">West Indies Federation</a>. It became an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies-associated-states">Associated State</a> in 1969 and gained independence, with the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a>, as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</a> on 27 October 1979.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1763 CE – 1979 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.79%;width:4.30%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1763 CE – 1979 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kingstown</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism and Methodism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and Vincentian Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Saint Vincent</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1871&amp;focus=colony-of-saint-vincent" aria-label="Colony of Saint Vincent on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3001 1688 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Saint Vincent lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M33